{"number":9,"title":"Solving One-Step Equations","slug":"solving-one-step-equations","color":"#14b8a6","level":"","estTime":"","description":"Grade 6 Maths: Solving One-Step Equations. Free study notes, solved examples, 10-question online test and 6 IMO practice questions on GrowQR.","topics":[{"title":"Solving Addition & Subtraction Equations","concept":"<p><strong>What is an Equation?</strong></p><p>An equation is a mathematical sentence that <strong>shows two expressions are equal</strong>. It has an equals sign (=).</p><p><strong>What does \"Solving\" mean?</strong></p><p>Solving means finding the value of the variable that makes the equation true.</p><p><strong>Inverse Operations:</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Operation</th><th>Inverse Operation</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Addition (+)</td><td>Subtraction (-)</td></tr><tr><td>Subtraction (-)</td><td>Addition (+)</td></tr><tr><td>Multiplication (×)</td><td>Division (÷)</td></tr><tr><td>Division (÷)</td><td>Multiplication (×)</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Golden Rule:</strong> Whatever you do to one side of the equation, you MUST do to the other side!</p>","visual":"<pre class=\"ascii-art\">SOLVING ADDITION EQUATION: x + 8 = 15\n\n    x + 8 = 15\n         │\n         ▼\n    Isolate x by subtracting 8 from BOTH sides\n         │\n         ▼\n    x + 8 - 8 = 15 - 8\n         │\n         ▼\n    x = 7\n    \n    Check: 7 + 8 = 15 ✓\n\n\nSOLVING SUBTRACTION EQUATION: y - 4 = 10\n\n    y - 4 = 10\n         │\n         ▼\n    Isolate y by adding 4 to BOTH sides\n         │\n         ▼\n    y - 4 + 4 = 10 + 4\n         │\n         ▼\n    y = 14\n    \n    Check: 14 - 4 = 10 ✓\n\n\nBALANCE SCALE MODEL:\n\n    Equation: x + 3 = 8\n    \n    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n    │                                 │\n    │   x + 3         8              │\n    │   ┌─┐┌─┐        ┌─┐            │\n    │   │ ││ │        │ │            │\n    │   │ ││ │        │ │            │\n    │   └─┘└─┘        └─┘            │\n    │   ════════════════════         │\n    │                                 │\n    └─────────────────────────────────┘\n    \n    Remove 3 from both sides:\n    \n    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n    │                                 │\n    │   x             5              │\n    │   ┌─┐          ┌─┐             │\n    │   │ │          │ │             │\n    │   │ │          │ │             │\n    │   └─┘          └─┘             │\n    │   ════════════════════         │\n    │                                 │\n    └─────────────────────────────────┘\n    \n    So x = 5</pre>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"<p>Solve: x + 8 = 15</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>To isolate x, subtract 8 from both sides</li><li>x + 8 - 8 = 15 - 8</li><li>x = 7</li><li>Answer: <strong>x = 7</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":2,"problem":"<p>Solve: y - 4 = 10</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>To isolate y, add 4 to both sides</li><li>y - 4 + 4 = 10 + 4</li><li>y = 14</li><li>Answer: <strong>y = 14</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":3,"problem":"<p>Solve: z + 12 = 25</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Subtract 12 from both sides</li><li>z + 12 - 12 = 25 - 12</li><li>z = 13</li><li>Answer: <strong>z = 13</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":4,"problem":"<p>Solve: a - 7 = 18</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Add 7 to both sides</li><li>a - 7 + 7 = 18 + 7</li><li>a = 25</li><li>Answer: <strong>a = 25</strong></li></ul>"}],"recap":["Isolate variable by using inverse operations","Addition → subtract from both sides","Subtraction → add to both sides","Check answer by substituting back"],"quiz":[{"q":"To solve $x+5=12$, you:","options":["add $5$","subtract $5$","multiply by $5$","divide by $5$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Subtract $5$."},{"q":"To solve $x-3=8$, you:","options":["subtract $3$","add $3$","multiply by $3$","divide by $3$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Add $3$."},{"q":"The solution of $x+4=9$ is:","options":["$4$","$5$","$13$","$9$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"$x=5$."},{"q":"Addition and subtraction are ___ operations.","options":["equal","inverse","same","prime"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Inverse."}]},{"title":"Solving Multiplication & Division Equations","concept":"<p><strong>Multiplication Equations:</strong></p><p>To solve 3z = 18, divide both sides by 3.</p><pre class=\"ascii-art\">3z = 18\n3z ÷ 3 = 18 ÷ 3\nz = 6</pre><p><strong>Division Equations:</strong></p><p>To solve m/2 = 7, multiply both sides by 2.</p><pre class=\"ascii-art\">m/2 = 7\nm/2 × 2 = 7 × 2\nm = 14</pre>","visual":"<pre class=\"ascii-art\">MULTIPLICATION EQUATION: 3z = 18\n\n    3z = 18 means 3 groups of z equal 18\n    \n    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n    │  ┌─┐┌─┐┌─┐                     │\n    │  │z││z││z│     18              │\n    │  └─┘└─┘└─┘                     │\n    │  ════════════════════         │\n    │                                 │\n    │  Divide both sides by 3:        │\n    │                                 │\n    │  ┌─┐                           │\n    │  │z│          6                │\n    │  └─┘                           │\n    │  ════════════════════         │\n    └─────────────────────────────────┘\n\n\nDIVISION EQUATION: m/2 = 7\n\n    m/2 = 7 means half of m equals 7\n    \n    ┌─────────────────────────────────┐\n    │                                 │\n    │     m                           │\n    │   ┌─┐                           │\n    │   │ │  half = 7                 │\n    │   │ │                           │\n    │   └─┘                           │\n    │   ════════════════════         │\n    │                                 │\n    │  Multiply both sides by 2:      │\n    │                                 │\n    │     m = 14                      │\n    │   ┌───┐                         │\n    │   │   │                         │\n    │   │   │                         │\n    │   └───┘                         │\n    │   ════════════════════         │\n    └─────────────────────────────────┘</pre>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"<p>Solve: 3z = 18</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Divide both sides by 3</li><li>3z ÷ 3 = 18 ÷ 3</li><li>z = 6</li><li>Answer: <strong>z = 6</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":2,"problem":"<p>Solve: m/2 = 7</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Multiply both sides by 2</li><li>(m/2) × 2 = 7 × 2</li><li>m = 14</li><li>Answer: <strong>m = 14</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":3,"problem":"<p>Solve: 5a = 35</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Divide both sides by 5</li><li>5a ÷ 5 = 35 ÷ 5</li><li>a = 7</li><li>Answer: <strong>a = 7</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":4,"problem":"<p>Solve: n/6 = 9</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Multiply both sides by 6</li><li>(n/6) × 6 = 9 × 6</li><li>n = 54</li><li>Answer: <strong>n = 54</strong></li></ul>"}],"recap":["Multiplication → divide both sides","Division → multiply both sides","Think: \"Do the opposite operation\"","Always check your answer"],"quiz":[{"q":"To solve $3x=12$, you:","options":["add $3$","divide by $3$","subtract $3$","multiply by $3$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Divide by $3$."},{"q":"To solve $\\tfrac{x}{4}=5$, you:","options":["divide by $4$","multiply by $4$","add $4$","subtract $4$"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Multiply by $4$."},{"q":"The solution of $5x=20$ is:","options":["$4$","$5$","$15$","$100$"],"correct":0,"explanation":"$x=4$."},{"q":"Multiplication and division are ___ operations.","options":["equal","inverse","same","prime"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Inverse."}]},{"title":"Checking Solutions by Substitution","concept":"<p><strong>Why Check Your Answer?</strong></p><p>Substituting your solution back into the original equation verifies that you solved correctly!</p><p><strong>Steps to Check:</strong></p><ol><li>Take the original equation</li><li>Replace the variable with your solution</li><li>Calculate both sides</li><li>If both sides are equal, your solution is correct!</li></ol><p><strong>Example:</strong> Solve x + 8 = 15 → x = 7</p><p>Check:</p><ul><li>Original: x + 8 = 15</li><li>Substitute x=7: 7 + 8 = 15</li><li>15 = 15 ✓ Correct!</li></ul>","visual":"<pre class=\"ascii-art\">CHECKING PROCESS - FLOWCHART:\n\n    Solve equation → Get solution\n           │\n           ▼\n    Substitute into original equation\n           │\n           ▼\n    Calculate left side and right side\n           │\n           ▼\n    Are they equal?\n         │\n    ┌────┴────┐\n    │         │\n   YES        NO\n    │         │\n    ▼         ▼\nCorrect   Check work\nsolution   and retry\n\n\nCHECKING MULTIPLICATION EQUATION:\n\n    Original: 3z = 18\n    Solution: z = 6\n    \n    Check: 3(6) = 18\n           18 = 18 ✓\n\n\nCHECKING DIVISION EQUATION:\n\n    Original: m/2 = 7\n    Solution: m = 14\n    \n    Check: 14/2 = 7\n           7 = 7 ✓\n\n\nCOMMON MISTAKES TO CHECK:\n\n    Mistake: x - 5 = 12 → x = 7 (should be 17)\n    Check: 7 - 5 = 2 ≠ 12 → Wrong!\n    \n    Mistake: 4x = 24 → x = 8 (should be 6)\n    Check: 4(8) = 32 ≠ 24 → Wrong!</pre>","examples":[{"number":1,"problem":"<p>Solve and check: x + 12 = 30</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Solve: x = 30 - 12 = 18</li><li>Check: 18 + 12 = 30 ✓</li><li>Answer: <strong>x = 18</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":2,"problem":"<p>Solve and check: y - 9 = 15</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Solve: y = 15 + 9 = 24</li><li>Check: 24 - 9 = 15 ✓</li><li>Answer: <strong>y = 24</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":3,"problem":"<p>Solve and check: 6a = 54</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Solve: a = 54 ÷ 6 = 9</li><li>Check: 6(9) = 54 ✓</li><li>Answer: <strong>a = 9</strong></li></ul>"},{"number":4,"problem":"<p>Solve and check: b/5 = 8</p>","solution":"<ul class=\"sol-list\"><li>Solve: b = 8 × 5 = 40</li><li>Check: 40/5 = 8 ✓</li><li>Answer: <strong>b = 40</strong></li></ul>"}],"recap":["Always check your solution by substituting back","Checks prevent careless mistakes","Both sides must be equal","If check fails, re-solve carefully","Show check work for full credit"],"quiz":[{"q":"To check a solution, you ___ it back into the equation.","options":["remove","substitute","double","ignore"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Substitute."},{"q":"If both sides are equal, the solution is:","options":["wrong","correct","zero","negative"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Correct."},{"q":"Does $x=4$ satisfy $2x+1=9$?","options":["Yes","No","Cannot say","Only sometimes"],"correct":0,"explanation":"$9=9$."},{"q":"A wrong solution makes the two sides:","options":["equal","unequal","zero","negative"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Unequal."}]}],"tests":{"online":{"title":"","minutes":15,"questions":[{"q":"x + 8 = 15","options":["x = ?","5","7","8"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"y - 4 = 10","options":["y = ?","6","14","40"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"3z = 18","options":["z = ?","3","6","9"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"m/2 = 7","options":["m = ?","3.5","9","14"],"correct":0,"explanation":"C","difficulty":"easy"},{"q":"a + 12 = 25","options":["a = ?","13","37","12"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"b - 7 = 18","options":["b = ?","11","25","24"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"5c = 35","options":["c = ?","5","7","30"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"n/4 = 9","options":["n = ?","36","2.25","13"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"x + 5 = 12","options":["x = ?","17","7","60"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"medium"},{"q":"8y = 64","options":["y = ?","8","512","56"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"medium"}]},"imo":{"title":"","minutes":10,"questions":[{"q":"x + 23 = 45","options":["x = ?","22","68","12"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"y - 15 = 28","options":["y = ?","13","43","420"],"correct":0,"explanation":"B","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"7z = 49","options":["z = ?","7","343","42"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"m/9 = 12","options":["m = ?","1.33","21","108"],"correct":0,"explanation":"C","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"4a + 3 = 23","options":["a = ?","5","6.5","20"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"hard"},{"q":"x/7 = 4","options":["x = ?","28","0.57","11"],"correct":0,"explanation":"A","difficulty":"hard"}]}}}